---
const config=JSON.stringify({mcpServers:{filesystem:{command:'npx',args:['-y','@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem','/ABSOLUTE/PATH/TO/ALLOWED/DIRECTORY']}}},null,2);
const source='https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/blob/main/src/filesystem/README.md';
---
<div class="guide"><p><strong>Maintainer-documented — not runtime tested by FreeMCP.</strong> Node.js 24+ required for npx installation. Claude Desktop uses a local stdio server.</p><p>Replace the sample absolute directory path with a real directory you explicitly want the server to access:</p><pre><code>{config}</code></pre><p><strong>Permissions:</strong> This server can read and modify files in allowed directories. For read-only access, insert <code>--read-only</code> before the directory argument. Use <code>--confine-roots</code> to prevent older MCP clients' Roots from widening access.</p><p>Windows: the maintainer documents launching npx through <code>cmd /c</code>. Do not grant access to home directories, credentials, or other sensitive paths unnecessarily.</p><a href={source} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Maintainer setup and access-control documentation ↗</a></div>
<style>.guide{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;padding:20px}.guide p{font-size:13px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--muted)}.guide strong{color:var(--text)}pre{padding:16px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;overflow:auto;font-size:12px}.guide a{color:var(--accent)}</style>